## **When Should You Consider Professional Mental Health Support?**

People seek therapy for many different reasons. You do not need to wait until a situation becomes overwhelming before considering professional support.

Speaking with a qualified therapist may be helpful if you are experiencing:

- Persistent feelings of sadness or emotional distress.
- Anxiety that interferes with everyday activities.
- Ongoing relationship or family conflicts.
- Difficulty managing stress at work or home.
- Grief following the loss of someone important.
- Challenges adjusting to major life changes.
- Emotional difficulties affecting sleep, concentration, or relationships.

A mental health professional can help you explore what you are experiencing and determine whether counseling or another form of support may be appropriate.

If you are experiencing immediate danger or a mental health emergency, call 911 or seek emergency assistance. In the United States, you can also call or text 988 for crisis support.

